{
  "_comment": "Split wire contract, shared byte for byte by every implementation. A results-log record has the key \"<partition>:<offset>\" (UTF-8) and goes to the results partition with the number of the source partition; its headers are log_header_order, each value ASCII text. Its value is compact JSON with sorted keys, raw UTF-8. A part record has the key and the value of the part, the source headers of the original message in their order minus every header whose name starts with \"dk-\", then the headers of part_header_order; dk-request-id is not written when the request id is null, and dk-split-sinks is written only when the origin is http (on or off). Part i goes to partition (offset mod N + i) mod N of the parts topic. Encoding of bytes in this file: a JSON string is its UTF-8 bytes, {\"base64\": \"...\"} is the decoded bytes, null is no value. The parsed form of a part case of origin kafka leaves deliver_sinks out: it is true for every such part.",
